ollowing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-15T19:56:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T19:56:07Z","body":"@clayjohn I assume we'll need to add a new limit:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/fa6b01802aa91e30f66a5646f9b5e3cda89eca2f/servers/rendering/rendering_device_commons.h#L975-L1021","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5687237067/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5687380851","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123478#issuecomment-5687380851","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123478","id":5687380851,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUv6Lcw","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-15T20:07:54Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T20:07:54Z","body":"I see, it is rounded down to the nearest supported by the driver, such as for Vulkan:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/be430ea73ad4c01ca0b90beb4ca4418c739408e8/drivers/vulkan/rendering_device_driver_vulkan.cpp#L2269-L2286","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5687380851/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5687714761","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123478#issuecomment-5687714761","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123478","id":5687714761,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUwOjyQ","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-15T20:35:03Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T20:35:03Z","body":"Well, MoltenVK does not work, so it sounds like there is something not being accounted for when the MSAA set by the rendering device does not match the rendering device driver","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5687714761/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5687777252","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123478#issuecomment-5687777252","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123478","id":5687777252,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUwSX5A","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-15T20:40:15Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T20:40:15Z","body":"Yep, suspicion confirmed. I had the 🤖 take a look, and it concluded the same thing. Basically the rendering engined doesn't know the driver changes the sample count, so it assumes the configured value, and that breaks assumptions. The 🤖 suggested a couple of options in the summary.\n\n<details>\n<summary>AI summary of root cause</summary>\n\nRoot cause: mismatch between requested and actual sample count, not the rounding itself.\n\n**What happens at 8x**\n\n1. `RenderSceneBuffersRD::configure` creates `RB_TEX_DEPTH_MSAA` with `TEXTURE_SAMPLES_8` (`render_scene_buffers_rd.cpp:198-200`).\n2. Metal driver silently rounds texture to 4 samples (`rendering_device_driver_metal.cpp:276`). Vulkan does same in `_ensure_supported_sample_count` (`rendering_device_driver_vulkan.cpp:2270`). Neither reports actual count back. `RD::texture_get_format` still says 8.\n3. Renderer resolves depth with `texture_multisamples[msaa]` = 8 (`render_forward_clustered.cpp:1807`, used at 2244/2349/2408/2485/2523, also `resolve_gi` at 2240).\n4. `resolve.glsl` `MODE_RESOLVE_DEPTH` loops `texelFetch(source_depth, pos, i)` for i in 0..7 on 4-sample texture. Samples 4..7 out of range: undefined, returns 0 on Metal. Sum divided by 8, so resolved depth roughly halved.\n5. Proximity fade reads `DEPTH_TEXTURE` = that resolved buffer. Garbage depth, fade breaks. 2x/4x fine because supported, no mismatch.\n\nRounding works. Problem: only drivers know rounding happened. Everything above driver assumes 8. MoltenVK same because Vulkan driver also rounds (M-series report max 4 through framebufferDepthSampleCounts).\n\n**Fix options**\n\n- Clamp at renderer level. Add `RD` query for max supported sample count (new `LIMIT_MAX_TEXTURE_SAMPLES` or similar, backed by `features.supportedSampleCounts` in Metal, `framebufferColorSampleCounts & framebufferDepthSampleCounts` in Vulkan). In `RenderSceneBuffersRD::configure`, clamp `msaa_3d` before use. Then pipelines, resolve shaders, `get_msaa_3d` all consistent. Smallest change, one place. Recommend this.\n- Alternative: store actual samples in RD texture record so `texture_get_format` reflects driver rounding, and renderer reads `texture_get_format(depth_msaa).samples` for resolve. Touches RDD interface, more surface.\n\nAlso mobile renderer passes `texture_multisamples` into `resolve_depth_raster`, same bug class; renderer-level clamp fixes both.\n\n</details>","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5687777252/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]